    <briefdescription>
<para>An analysis for type-inference for VPValues. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It infers the scalar type for a given <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_v_p_value" kindref="compound">VPValue</ref> by bottom-up traversing through defining recipes until root nodes with known types are reached (e.g. live-ins or load recipes). The types are then propagated top down through operations. Note that the analysis caches the inferred types. A new analysis object must be constructed once a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_v_plan" kindref="compound">VPlan</ref> has been modified in a way that invalidates any of the previously inferred types. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
